# Code owners — travel-planner
#
# Single-maintainer model: the repository owner owns all paths. On a public
# repository this routes a review request to the owner on every pull request;
# external contributors can propose changes via fork PRs but cannot merge.
# Required-code-owner-review is intentionally NOT enforced as a hard branch-
# protection gate (a solo owner cannot approve their own PR — that would self-
# lock the repo). Enforcement of "owner-only merge" comes from branch protection
# (PR required + CI gate) plus the absence of other write collaborators.

